# Review: mesh/sent start arity (dart-dht-profile, uncommitted, 2 files +13/−11)

Read-only review performed against `git diff` in this worktree (master a4efc99a). No files edited, no suites run.

## Findings

**No actionable findings.**

Non-blocking observations (not defects of this diff, no fix requested):

- P3 | test/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc:211 | five more call sites (`:211`, `:234`, `:249`, `:322`, `:362`) and `mesh/sent-from` (test/dao/jing/dht/mesh.cljc:266) still decode the whole log per call, the very pattern this diff removes from the hot loop | none — behavior-unchanged is the requirement; the new `(sent net start)` arity is a ready-made fix if any of these ever grows a comparable loop.

## Check 1 — `(sent net)` identity and the `:log` vector invariant

- One-arg delegates to `(sent net 0)` (test/dao/jing/dht/mesh.cljc:226); the mapped fn body at mesh.cljc:228-234 is the old body verbatim (same keys `:from :to :size :bytes :message`, same order), and `mapv` returns a vector on all hosts — return type is a vector before and after.
- On cljd, `(subvec v 0)` hits the `(and (zero? start) (== end n)) v` fast path and returns `v` itself; JVM/CLJS return a view. In every case `mapv` builds a fresh vector of the same elements in the same order — observably identical.
- `:log` invariant holds repo-wide: seeded `[]` (mesh.cljc:48); the only writers anywhere are `swap! net update :log conj` at mesh.cljc:78 (MeshSocket `append!`) and mesh.cljc:114 (seam's `send!`) — `conj` onto a persistent vector stays a vector on JVM, CLJS and cljd. Repo-wide grep finds no test reseeding or dissoc'ing `:log` on a mesh atom: dht_test's net swaps touch only `:refuse-datagram?` (dht_test.cljc:1101) and `:drop-datagram?` (:1153) plus mesh-internal `:traffic`/`:held`/`:drop?`/`:refuse?`/`:hold?`; the `:log` hits elsewhere (yin/vm/macro_test.cljc:319…, dao/stream/observer_test.cljc:501, dao/stream/udp_test.cljc:34) are unrelated atoms. `subvec` can never see a list, lazy seq, or nil.
- `start == size` → empty vector on all three hosts (sources below). `start > size` → throws (JVM `IndexOutOfBoundsException`, CLJS `js/Error`, cljd `ArgumentError`) — acceptable, because the only two-arg call site in the repo is dht_test.cljc:1201 and its sole `start` source is `(mesh/log-size net)` (grep-verified; the other call is the literal `0`).

## Check 2 — loop equivalence

- dht_test.cljc:1198-1201: `inject!` writes only the traffic ring (dht_test.cljc:169-179, no `:log` write), `before` is `(mesh/log-size net)`, then `(dht/step s 1)` runs, then `(mesh/sent net before)` reads `(:log @net)` post-step — the exact snapshot the old `(drop before (mesh/sent net))` read. The log is append-only and the test single-threaded, so entries `0..before-1` are precisely the pre-step entries and the two forms select the same elements in the same order.
- `replies` is consumed only by `(count replies)` (:1204, :1209) and `(every? … replies)` (:1205-1206). On a vector both are value-identical to their lazy-seq behavior (count becomes O(1)); no seq-specific operation (`first`/`rest`/nil-punning-as-seq) exists in the loop. Final assertions at :1210-1212 are untouched — the diff changes only the binding line.

## Check 3 — all other callers

Every remaining call site uses the one-arg arity, unchanged: dht_test.cljc `:211`, `:234`, `:249`, `:261`, `:286`, `:319`, `:322`, `:362`, `:473`, `:1043`, `:1048`, `:1052`, `:1060`; `mesh/sent-from` callers dht_test.cljc:1012 and test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:545 (sent-from internally calls `(sent net)`, mesh.cljc:266). No `mesh/sent` reference exists under `src/`. Per check 1, one-arg output is bit-identical to the old function.

## Check 4 — portability, verified from the exact pinned toolchains

- JVM (clojure-1.12.4): `RT.subvec` bytecode — throws `IndexOutOfBoundsException` when `end<start`/`start<0`/`end>count`; `start==end` returns `PersistentVector.EMPTY`.
- Node (CLJS 1.12.42 via shadow-cljs 3.3.5, deps.edn:40): `cljs/core.cljs:6120-6142` — `(subvec v start)` defaults `end` to `(count v)`; `build-subvec` throws `js/Error "Index out of bounds"` on the same checks **and** requires `(vector? v)` (the invariant from check 1 is load-bearing here and holds); `start==end` yields an empty Subvec that `mapv` consumes normally.
- Dart (cljd pin `23576fbe…`, deps.edn:56-61): `clj/src/cljd/core.cljd:4181-4202` — identical bound checks (`ArgumentError`), `(zero? start) (== end n)` fast path, `start==end` → `[]`; `ISubvecable` is implemented by `PersistentVector` (core.cljd:3946), which is what `:log` always is; `count`'s int passes `.toInt` cleanly.
- Precedent: 2-arg `subvec` on persistent vectors already runs green on all three lanes (e.g. src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1459, src/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:188, src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:383).

